,title,link,text,language,family
0,Wagiman - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wagiman,"April 3, 2024 - The Wagiman, also spelt Wagoman, Wagaman, Wogeman, and other variants, are an Aboriginal Australian people of the Northern Territory.",Wagiman,Australian
1,Wagiman language - Wikipedia,https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wagiman_language,"September 3, 2025 - Wagiman, also spelt Wageman, Wakiman, Wogeman, and other variants, is a near-extinct Aboriginal Australian language spoken by only two elderly people, who live in and around Pine Creek, in the Katherine Region of the Northern Territory.",Wagiman,Australian
2,"Wagaman, Northern Territory","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wagaman,_Northern_Territory","January 26, 2026 - Wagaman is named after the Wagiman Aboriginal tribe from present-day Pine Creek, in the Katherine Region of the Northern Territory.",Wagiman,Australian
3,Wageman - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wageman,"October 23, 2021 - The Wagiman, also spelt Wageman, an Aboriginal Australian people · Wagiman language, also spelt Wageman, an Aboriginal Australian language · Wagemans · Categories: Disambiguation pages · Disambiguation pages with surname-holder lists · Search · Wageman ·",Wagiman,Australian
4,Wagiman,https://aiatsis.gov.au/austlang/language/n27,Australian Capital Territory · New South Wales · Northern Territory · Queensland · South Australia · Tasmania · Victoria · Western Australia · Collection · Search the Collection · Featured collections · A.M. Fernando notebooks · Musical Connections: Alice Moyle ·,Wagiman,Australian
5,"""Wagiman online dictionary""",https://aphasialab.org/wagiman/,"Wagiman is an Australian Aboriginal language spoken in Australia's Northern Territory. On this web site you will find an online dictionary of Wagiman, as well as some general information about the language and its speakers, three texts, and some links and references to more material on Wagiman ...",Wagiman,Australian
6,WAGIMAN. : languagehat.com,https://languagehat.com/wagiman/,"There are several dialects of Wagiman, with the most prominent distinction being between matjjin no-roh-ma ‘light language’ and matjjin gu-nawutj-jan ‘heavy language’. Helen Liddy and Lenny Liddy speak light language, and Lulu Martin, Paddy Huddlestone and Clara McMahon speak heavy language. There is not all that much difference, and no Wagiman speakers have any trouble understanding one another.",Wagiman,Australian
7,Wagiman facts for kids,https://kids.kiddle.co/Wagiman,"October 17, 2025 - The Wagiman people are an Aboriginal Australian group from the Northern Territory in Australia. You might also see their name spelled as Wagoman, Wagaman, or Wogeman.",Wagiman,Australian
8,Wagiman online dictionary | Australian Aboriginal Languages Student Blog,https://australianlanguages.wordpress.com/2012/07/23/wagiman-online-dictionary/,"July 23, 2012 - Wagiman is a highly endangered language from the Northern Territory. This website holds a Wagiman dictionary as well as background information including genetic,phonological and morphological information, texts, and a page of links and references. It doesn't look like it has been updated recently, but is a great resource nonetheless.",Wagiman,Australian
9,"""Wagiman online dictionary - The language and its speakers""",https://aphasialab.org/wagiman/langspeakers.html,"Wagiman is an Australian Aboriginal language spoken in Australia's Northern Territory. At the moment there are about ten people who speak Wagiman, mostly old people. Wagiman belongs to what linguists call the non-Pama-Nyungan language family.",Wagiman,Australian
